    "BrochureContent": [
      {
        "ContentType": "Description",
        "SortOrder": 0,
        "Content": "Dooley Poynton Auctioneers are delighted to present this superb split level detached family residence situated in a highly sought after & desirable residential development. This property enjoys a superb, elevated position commanding unrivalled panoramic views of the Sugar Loaf Mountain and Wicklow’s Coastline. The property is in showhouse condition throughout. It is evident that no expense has been spared to maximise the comfort and style that this dream home exudes. The accommodation comprises of a welcoming entrance hallway leading to an elegant living room with stunning sea views. This level also features a guest w/c & utility room. The first floor showcases a bright and spacious contemporary designed open plan kitchen/dining room overlooking the secluded south facing landscaped rear garden. On the upper levels the property features four well-appointed bedrooms with master ensuite and a family bathroom. This unique home offers something for every member of the family with a host of leisure amenities including Wicklow Tennis Club, Coral Leisure Centre, Wicklow Harbour and Wicklow Golf Club. There is an excellent selection of primary and secondary schools nearby Wicklow Educate Together national school and Colaiste Chill Mhantain, secondary school. There are excellent nearby commuter links with easy access to the N11/M11 and Wicklow train station serving Dublin City Centre."
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Accommodation",
        "SortOrder": 1,
        "Content": "Entrance Hallway (4.85m x 2.93m)\r\nThis attractively designed split level hallway has porcelain tiled flooring, a stylish radiator cover, recessed ceiling lights. This space also houses the alarm panel and has walnut panel doors to the living room, utility & guest WC. A solid walnut tread staircase leads up to the open plan kitchen/dining room. \r\n\r\nGuest W/C (2.08m x 1.68m)\r\nThe large guest WC features a vanity wash hand basin with storage, a mirror and light & a toilet. This space has tastefully tiled flooring with partially tiled walls.\r\n\r\nCloak/Utility Room (2.35m x 2.51m)\r\nThis spacious cloak room/utility room features a Whirlpool washing machine, a Whirlpool dryer and a Hoover Freezer. This room houses the Immergas Combi Boiler and providing ample storage space.\r\n\r\nLiving Room (5.12m x 4.72m)\r\nThis bright and spacious elegant living room boasts a large window framing the magnificent sea & mountain views and overlooks the front garden area. This room features a wood burning stove set into a polished sandstone fireplace with granite hearth and surround. The room inset lighting and has luxury cream carpet throughout. \r\n\r\nKitchen/Dining Room (3.52m x 9.47m)\r\nAt the heart of the home is a generously proportioned open plan kitchen/dining room. Situated to the rear of the property this space fully embraces the concept of zonal, modern family living. This room is infused with natural sunlight with French doors open out into the beautiful south facing patio and garden area. The contemporary bespoke kitchen is fitted with numerous high & low units along with a centre island/breakfast bar with Quartz worktops. There are many fine features and high spec integrated appliances including a ceramic Whirlpool induction hob, double eye level Hotpoint oven, extractor, fridge/freezer and Whirlpool dishwasher. There is also a glass splash-back, inset lighting and numerous polished chrome electrical sockets. The room has a stylish radiator cover & porcelain tiled floor throughout. The dining area has ample space for a large dining table and chairs.\r\n\r\nMaster Bedroom 1 (4.42m x 4.72m) \r\nThe master bedroom is situated to the front of the property and has magnificent sea and coastal views of Wicklow. This room is tastefully decorated in a neutral colour palette, featuring high angled ceilings and has luxury carpeted flooring throughout. \r\n\r\nWalk-in Wardrobe (2.36m x 1.64m)\r\nThe walk-in wardrobe is fully fitted with walnut shelving and clothing hanging rails.\r\n\r\nEnsuite (1.28m x 2.98m)\r\nThe fully tiled en-suite has a walk-in shower unit with a pumped rain shower, a vanity wash hand basin with shaving light and mirror, extractor fan and WC.\r\n\r\nBedroom 2 (3.52m x 4.19m)\r\nThe second guest bedroom has a large window along with to two Velux windows flooding the room with natural light and is fitted with floor to ceiling built-in slide robes. This room has eaves storage, a TV point & numerous sockets and is fully carpeted throughout.\r\n\r\nBedroom 3 (3.52m x 3.33m)\r\nThe guest bedroom is located on the second level overlooking the south facing rear of the property. It has floor to ceiling built in wardrobes and is fully carpeted. There is also access to the eaves storage, ample electric sockets and a TV point.\r\n\r\nBedroom 4 (4.58m x 2.61m)\r\nThis first floor guest bedroom embraces stunning sea views and is currently being used as a study. It is fully carpeted throughout and has a TV point and numerous sockets.\r\n\r\nFamily Bathroom (2.56m x 2.13m)\r\nThis bathroom is fully tiled throughout & boasts a large bath with a separate walk-in shower unit with pumped shower. There is also a vanity wash hand basin with mirror, lighting and a walnut cabinet with additional storage, an extractor fan, a W.C. and inset lighting throughout.\r\n\r\nFront/Rear Garden \r\nThe property is approached via an elegant cobble lock driveway. The front and rear gardens have been tastefully landscaped with flower beds, plum trees, ash trees, hydrangea and an array of mature plants & shrubs. This secluded south facing rear garden has walled boundaries and provides dual access to the front of the property via wrought iron gates. The large rear patio area is paved with Italian stone slabs, the large lawned area gives the garden a contemporary feel, providing a fantastic outdoor living space. The garden features exterior incandescent lighting, an outdoor tap, security lighting & a garden shed located to the side of the property.\r\n\r\nServices: \r\n•\tGas Fired Central Heating\r\n•\tMains Water\r\n•\tMains Sewerage\r\n•\tFibre Broadband\r\n•\tFully Alarmed\r\n•\tBER A3, BER NO: 110205010  (57.49kWh/m2/yr)"
      },
      {
        "ContentType": "Features",
        "SortOrder": 3,
        "Content": "•\tEnviable site with unrivalled sea and coastal views of Wicklow’s Coastline.\r\n•\tOne of the Most Sought-After Low-Density Family Developments in Wicklow Town. \r\n•\tSuperb Four Bedroom Detached Family Home with State-of-the-Art Appliances.\r\n•\tIn Showhouse Condition with a South Facing Landscaped Rear Garden.\r\n•\tPhotovoltaic solar panels. \r\n•\tClose to all Local Amenities, Shops and Schools."
      },
